 "drivingQuestion": "Whose view does the practice of moving handleless oven covers follow?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Ravina identifies local practice with R' Eliezer ben Ya'akov",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.125a.15",
   "daf": "125a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "הֵעִיד רַבִּי יוֹסֵי מִשּׁוּם רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב עַל שִׁבְרֵי תַּנּוּר יָשָׁן שֶׁנִּיטָּלִין בַּשַּׁבָּת, וְעַל כִּיסּוּיוֹ שֶׁאֵינוֹ צָרִיךְ בֵּית יָד. אָמַר רָבִינָא: כְּמַאן מְטַלְטְלִינַן הָאִידָּנָא כִּיסּוּי דְּתַנּוּרֵי דְמָתָא מַחְסֵיָא דְּאֵין לָהֶם בֵּית אֲחִיזָה? כְּמַאן — כְּרַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב.",
   "en": "In that same Tosefta where «Rabbi Yosei testified in the name of Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov about shards of an old oven that may be moved on Shabbat, and about its cover, which does not require a handle,» and which is considered a vessel and may be moved as is, «Ravina says: In accordance with whose» opinion «do we now move the oven covers» in «the city of Meḥasya that do not have handles? In accordance with whose» opinion is it? It is «in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov.»"
  }
 ],
